---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
One combined view of pinned PRs, upstream changes, ports, updates and drift

Usage: odx dashboard [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  act   Take one entry's action
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (`--json` overrides it)

          Possible values:
          - table:    Terminal table
          - tui:      Interactive terminal UI (in builds with the `tui` feature: `cargo install odx-cli --features tui`)
          - markdown: Markdown, as used for the dashboard issue
          
          [default: table]

      --env <ENV>
          Environment to show; defaults to all

      --section <SECTION>
          Only these sections (pinned, droppable, new-upstream, forward-port, backport, auto-update, glue, drift, suppressed)

      --checkboxes
          With `--format markdown`, a box per action for the bot to read back

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only; a repository not in the cache yet is still fetched. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only
